\newlabel{fig:t0}{{3a}{7}{Causality Bubbles in Orbital Engagements. This subfigure represents two independent orbital engagements, where teams of satellites interact within localized causality bubbles. These bubbles correspond to Figure 1’s perigee and apogee engagements, demonstrating how spatial separation allows for independent evolution. Blue and Red have marshaled their resources and the engagement begins at $t_{0}$. The engagements unfold independently, with no need for global synchronization.\relax }{figure.caption.8}{}}
\newlabel{fig:t0@cref}{{[subfigure][1][3]3a}{[1][6][]7}}
\newlabel{sub@fig:t0}{{a}{7}{Causality Bubbles in Orbital Engagements. This subfigure represents two independent orbital engagements, where teams of satellites interact within localized causality bubbles. These bubbles correspond to Figure 1’s perigee and apogee engagements, demonstrating how spatial separation allows for independent evolution. Blue and Red have marshaled their resources and the engagement begins at $t_{0}$. The engagements unfold independently, with no need for global synchronization.\relax }{figure.caption.8}{}}
\newlabel{sub@fig:t0@cref}{{[subfigure][1][3]3a}{[1][6][]7}}
\newlabel{fig:tf}{{3b}{7}{Combat Resolution and Team-Level Status Update at $t_{f}$. This subfigure captures the immediate aftermath of the engagement, where satellite losses are identified (grayed-out units), and battle outcomes are reported to the orchestrator module. Each image team maintains local autonomy while synchronizing only when necessary, ensuring that engagement results are efficiently communicated without imposing unnecessary global synchronization.\relax }{figure.caption.8}{}}
\newlabel{fig:tf@cref}{{[subfigure][2][3]3b}{[1][6][]7}}
\newlabel{sub@fig:tf}{{b}{7}{Combat Resolution and Team-Level Status Update at $t_{f}$. This subfigure captures the immediate aftermath of the engagement, where satellite losses are identified (grayed-out units), and battle outcomes are reported to the orchestrator module. Each image team maintains local autonomy while synchronizing only when necessary, ensuring that engagement results are efficiently communicated without imposing unnecessary global synchronization.\relax }{figure.caption.8}{}}
\newlabel{sub@fig:tf@cref}{{[subfigure][2][3]3b}{[1][6][]7}}
\newlabel{fig:tlater}{{3c}{7}{Formation of New Teams for Mission-Level Objectives. At a much later simulation stage, surviving assets have been reorganized into new teams, assigned to mission-level engagements based on the orchestrator’s strategic objectives. This restructuring ensures that computational resources are aligned with evolving mission needs, mirroring real-world operational planning. The transition from localized causality bubbles to higher-level coordination exemplifies how Coarray Fortran’s image teams scale seamlessly from tactical engagements to strategic mission execution.\relax }{figure.caption.8}{}}
\newlabel{fig:tlater@cref}{{[subfigure][3][3]3c}{[1][6][]7}}
\newlabel{sub@fig:tlater}{{c}{7}{Formation of New Teams for Mission-Level Objectives. At a much later simulation stage, surviving assets have been reorganized into new teams, assigned to mission-level engagements based on the orchestrator’s strategic objectives. This restructuring ensures that computational resources are aligned with evolving mission needs, mirroring real-world operational planning. The transition from localized causality bubbles to higher-level coordination exemplifies how Coarray Fortran’s image teams scale seamlessly from tactical engagements to strategic mission execution.\relax }{figure.caption.8}{}}
\newlabel{sub@fig:tlater@cref}{{[subfigure][3][3]3c}{[1][6][]7}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Physical Engagement and Computational Parallelism: A Unified Perspective. This figure illustrates the direct mapping between real-world orbital engagements and their computational representation. The first subfigure shows physical satellite formations evolving within causality bubbles. Physical causality is respected while maximizing computational efficiency. This direct mapping between physics and computation enables scalable, high-fidelity simulations of multi-agent engagements in orbital environments.\relax }}{7}{figure.caption.8}\protected@file@percent }
